    (titleSlide.live/updating/stale/offline/refresh/retry/loading/noData/emptyHint/
    errorTitle/staleBanner/offlineBanner) all present in TitleSlide.strings. No English
    literal in Swift (Text(verbatim:) only wraps facade-resolved strings + the decorative
    emoji + the em-dash sentinel).
  a11y -> the hero is ONE combined VoiceOver element speaking the pure
    TitleSlideAccessibility.summary ("Year in Review, 2,026, <vehicle>"); the emoji + the
    error icon are accessibilityHidden; the freshness chip / refresh / retry controls each
    carry an accessibilityLabel; Dynamic Type via tokens; Reduce Motion gates the hero
    scale entrance, the TSFadeIn stagger, and the skeleton shimmer.
  telemetry -> TitleSlideModel.start() emits viewOpened(surface:"TitleSlide") -> bridges
