=== YEAR-GROUPING PARITY NOTE (deliberate, pinned) ===
  The web year glyph is `<AnimatedNumber value={data.year} />`, whose default decimals=0
  feeds fmtNumber(year, 0) -> value.toLocaleString(locale, {min/maxFractionDigits:0}).
  For a four-digit year that EMITS a grouping separator (en-US -> "2,026"). Per the Honesty
  Covenant (no silent drift / no parity shortcuts) and the YearReviewWidget.Adapter
  precedent ("reproduce the web call chain verbatim rather than correcting it"), the native
  adapter reproduces this EXACTLY — TitleSlideFormat.year(2026,"en_US") == "2,026" — so a
  user with the web and native recaps open side by side sees identical text. Pinned by
  TitleSlideAdapterTests.testYearGroupsLikeWebFmtNumber (+ locale + sub-threshold cases).

